From 9a27c904f10653649df6147ef413f49231038b94 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: permissionBRICK <40219477+permissionBRICK@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 13:58:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] tpm: add a driver for the Qualcomm X1E firmware TPM
 (qcom.tz.tpm)

Snapdragon X Elite (X1E80100) laptops ship a firmware TPM 2.0 that runs as
the QSEE application "qcom.tz.tpm" in TrustZone. On Windows the ACPI TPM2
table describes it with the vendor start method 9: TPM commands go through
a TCG Command Response Buffer (CRB) in memory shared with TrustZone, and a
QSEECOM request to the application runs a pending command. Linux boots
these machines with a devicetree, so there is no TPM2 table and no TPM.

The application protocol (as used by the TPM service of Qualcomm's Windows
TrEE driver): every request starts with a little-endian command id.
  0x1000   application version, must be 1.0
  0x80000  TPM type, 0x6654504d ("fTPM")
  0x4012   CRB location: { word, address low, address high }
  0x4008   run the command in the CRB: request { 0x4008, 0x400 } padded
           to 0x408 bytes, response 0x404 bytes; the application clears
           the CRB start bit when the response is in place.

The driver looks the application up over QSEECOM, checks version and type,
maps the CRB the application reports and registers a synchronous TPM 2.0
chip. The application's QSEECOM interface is the legacy one; the QCOMTEE
object service "qcom.tz.tpm" (UID 81) used by newer platforms is not
exposed by the X1E80100 firmware (QTEE 5.2.0).

Tested on an ASUS Vivobook S 15 (S5507QA): QCOM "xCGfTPM" TPM 2.0 rev 1.62,
firmware 4.0.0.1; PCRs 0-7 match the replay of the firmware event log;
works across suspend/resume.
---
 drivers/char/tpm/Kconfig        |  15 ++
 drivers/char/tpm/Makefile       |   1 +
 drivers/char/tpm/tpm_qcom_crb.c | 298 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 314 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 drivers/char/tpm/tpm_qcom_crb.c

diff --git a/drivers/char/tpm/Kconfig b/drivers/char/tpm/Kconfig
index 5f672f2c0..48aadc618 100644
--- a/drivers/char/tpm/Kconfig
+++ b/drivers/char/tpm/Kconfig
@@ -243,6 +243,21 @@ config TCG_FTPM_TEE
 	help
 	  This driver proxies for firmware TPM running in TEE.
 
+config TCG_QCOM_CRB
+	tristate "Qualcomm X1E firmware TPM (qcom.tz.tpm, CRB interface)"
+	depends on ARCH_QCOM || COMPILE_TEST
+	depends on QCOM_QSEECOM
+	help
+	  Driver for the firmware TPM of Snapdragon X Elite (X1E80100) laptops.
+	  The TPM runs as the QSEE application "qcom.tz.tpm" in TrustZone and
+	  is reached through a TCG Command Response Buffer shared with the
+	  secure world (ACPI TPM2 start method 9 on Windows). The kernel boots
+	  these machines with a devicetree, so the driver locates the buffer
+	  through the application and needs no firmware description.
+
+	  To compile this driver as a module, choose M here; the module will
+	  be called tpm_qcom_crb.
+
 config TCG_SVSM
 	tristate "SNP SVSM vTPM interface"
 	depends on AMD_MEM_ENCRYPT
